-- title:
--   Weight-two form with simple poles at two prescribed points
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$; write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, the image in $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ sending $\gamma$ to its lower-right entry mod $M$. Let $F_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), the $q$-expansion function field attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$ inside the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\mathbb{C}F_0$ be its base change [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $\mathbb{C}$-subfield of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of $F_0$. Let $D$ be a complex place dictionary for $(\Gamma_H(M), F_0)$: a map $\mathrm{pt}$ from $\mathfrak{H}$ to the places of $\mathbb{C}F_0$ over $\mathbb{C}$ together with a positive integer-valued ramification function $e$, such that $\mathrm{pt}$ is $\Gamma_H(M)$-invariant, the valuation subring of $\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ consists exactly of those $x$ whose realization $\mathrm{realizeOf}$ is bounded on a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$, and the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of the realization of a nonzero $x$ equals $e(\tau) \cdot \mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{pt}(\tau)}(x)$. Assume $\tau_1, \tau_2 \in \mathfrak{H}$ satisfy $\mathrm{pt}(\tau_1) \ne \mathrm{pt}(\tau_2)$. Then there exist a function $\omega : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ and a finitely supported function $r$ from the places of $\mathbb{C}F_0$ over $\mathbb{C}$ to $\mathbb{C}$ such that: $\omega \mid[2] \gamma = \omega$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(M)$; for every $\sigma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ there is $\delta > 0$ with $\omega \mid[2] \sigma = O(e^{-\delta \operatorname{Im} \tau})$ as $\operatorname{Im}\tau \to \infty$; $r(\mathrm{pt}(\tau_1)) \ne 0$; every place $P$ with $r(P) \ne 0$ equals $\mathrm{pt}(\tau_1)$ or $\mathrm{pt}(\tau_2)$; and for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ there is a function $g$ analytic at $\tau$ with $\omega(z) = e(\tau)\, r(\mathrm{pt}(\tau))/(z - \tau) + g(z)$ for all $z$ in a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$ in $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the Riemann–Roch existence statement $\Omega(P+Q) \supsetneq \Omega(Q)$ on the modular curve $X_H(M)$ — a differential of the third kind with a genuine simple pole at one prescribed point, at most a simple pole at a second, and holomorphic elsewhere including the cusps (whence the exponential decay of all $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$-translates) — transported to a weight-two invariant function on the upper half-plane via the place dictionary $D$; no condition is imposed on the residue at $\mathrm{pt}(\tau_2)$. It feeds the companion statement [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.exists_slashInvariant_residue_eq_of_degree_eq_zero_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.exists_slashInvariant_residue_eq_of_degree_eq_zero_gammaH), where the residue theorem pins the two residues against one another.
